# Transforms - the meta-language extension describing conversions between yamlover shapes.
# A future-facing chapter: the named transforms are hardcoded today, written out later.
Transforms
description: an extension of meta - conversions between yamlover shapes, typed at both ends
- '*Status: design - this layer is not implemented yet.*'
- >
  A **transform** converts between shapes of yamlover data. It is the lower-level, data-to-data
  counterpart of the [projection](*::language:model:terminology) the engine serves: a projection is
  the read-side view of storage, a transform reshapes data into data.
- >
  Transforms are an **extension of the meta language** ([yamlover meta](*::meta)). The meta
  language can describe transforms between various shapes of yamlover, and a transform reads like
  a **function prototype**: a meta for the **arguments** - the accepted input shapes - and a meta
  for the **result** - the produced shape - plus the information that describes the data
  conversion and reshaping between the two.
- >
  Several familiar names are reserved as **names of transforms**: `!!omap` and `!!pairs` (a mapping
  reshaped into ordered `[key, value]` members and back), and `!!binary` (bytes decoded into a
  value and encoded back). The frame is `!!yo`'s ([named metas](*::language:model:meta)): a
  transform is a meta, so a bare `!!name` may equally name one, and the name is all the surface
  ever shows.
